<usx version="3.0"><chapter style="c" number="4" sid=" 4"/><para style="cl">Chapter Four</para><para style="cd">This chapter description (cd) follows the chapter label (cl). Chapter 4 exercises standard USFM that chapters 1 through 3 do not use, plus shapes that pin known converter bugs. Chapter 5 holds deliberately damaged USFM.</para><para style="s1">A section heading before verse 1</para><para style="r">(2 Sam 4.1-12)</para><para style="b"/><para style="p"><verse style="v" number="1" sid=""/>A cross reference<note style="x" caller="+"><char style="xo" closed="false">4.1: </char><char style="xt" closed="false">1 Sam 31.4; 2 Sam 1.1</char></note> sits mid-verse. This verse ends with a footnote butted against the next verse marker with no space between them.<note style="f" caller="+"><char style="fr" closed="false">4.1 </char><char style="ft" closed="false">A footnote that ends right before the next verse marker.</char></note> <verse style="v" number="2-3" pubnumber="2-3a" sid=""/> Verse bridge 2-3 carrying a published verse number (vp). <verse style="v" number="4a" sid=""/>Verse segment 4a. <verse style="v" number="4b" sid=""/>Verse segment 4b. <verse style="v" number="5" sid=""/>An endnote<note style="fe" caller="+"><char style="fr" closed="false">4.5 </char><char style="ft" closed="false">Endnote text.</char></note> then a footnote with no caller<note style="f" caller="-"><char style="fr" closed="false">4.5 </char><char style="ft" closed="false">The minus caller means no caller is shown.</char></note> then one with a custom caller<note style="f" caller="a"><char style="fr" closed="false">4.5 </char><char style="ft" closed="false">Custom caller a.</char></note> end. <verse style="v" number="6" sid=""/>Non-breaking spaces: a character span whose whole content is a NBSP <char style="nd"> </char>, one with a leading NBSP <char style="nd"> lead</char>, one with a trailing NBSP <char style="nd">trail </char>, a NBSP before punctuation mot : and one inside a number 1 000.</para><para style="p" vid=""> </para><para style="p" vid="">The paragraph above has a lone NBSP as its only content. This paragraph ends with a space before an unknown marker </para><para style="zunk" vid="">Unknown marker content.</para><para style="p" vid="">Authored references: a closed </para><para style="ref">1 Sam 1.1|1SA 1:1<unmatched marker="ref*"/> and an unclosed </para><para style="ref">1 Sam 2.1|1SA 2:1 that runs to the end of the paragraph.</para><chapter eid=" 4"/></usx>